From 3ef0bbd0c2ef5fc4e272a12d61b9633f66ac2483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Shearman <georgemog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:02:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] zz9000: accelerated P96 driver for the Minimig Z3 RTG
 board

Port of the official ZZ9000 RTG stack to the MiSTer Minimig core, with
no FPGA changes: the ZZ9000OS blitter runs on the HPS inside the MiSTer
binary and draws into the existing Z3 RTG framebuffer (DDR3 0x27000000).

Amiga side, MiSTerZZ.card (amiga/rtg/mntgfx-gcc.c):
- finds the $139C/$30 RTG board; P96 gets the bottom $7C0000, the top
  256KB holds mailbox, GFXData, staging and the mouse save buffer
- accelerated hooks are the upstream Z3 paths; the blitter_dma_op
  doorbell becomes a synchronous mailbox kick, with CacheClearU() around
  the wait because cpu_cache_new caches the RTG window
- display hooks program rtg.v as MiSTer.card does; ZZ9000-only features
  (sprite, capture, split, DPMS, offscreen, PIP) are not offered
- falls back to P96 software routines when no ARM blitter answers
- MiSTerZZInfo: read-only bring-up/status tool

MiSTer side (mister/, installed into Main_MiSTer by install.py):
- upstream gfx.c unmodified, built via a wrapper that avoids unaligned,
  NEON and libc string accesses on the Strongly-ordered /dev/mem mapping
- dma_rtg.c adapted: private GFXData snapshot, range checks on every
  Amiga-supplied offset, display/sprite/overlay ops dropped
- service thread with spin-then-sleep polling and session handshake

Shared protocol in common/mister_zz9000.h. Host test (tests/host) runs
the exact ARM code against independent reference renderers: 241 checks
pass under ASan/UBSan. Card, info tool and a full MiSTer binary build on
the build server. Not yet run on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
